theory/soft-index.md:449:> 1. Fix D10's complexified broken charge/current, `I=[a,b]\Subset(0,\pi)`, normalized `\eta,f\in C_c^\infty` with `\int\eta=1` and `\|f\|_2=1`, and regulators `\lambda=(N,W,T,\sigma,\varsigma)`: periodic ring, seam-separated finite window, on-shell filter, hard-packet width, and soft-resolution width.  The hard packet has carrier `h\in I` and width `\sigma`.  The finite filter is `\Pi_{N,T}(E)=\int T^{-1}\eta(t/T)e^{it(H_N-E)}dt`.  Window-local preparation/resolution matrices, followed by `\Pi_{N,T}` and the momentum filters, give `L^2(I)` connected pairings `M_{1,\lambda}^{(h)}` and `M_{2,\lambda}^{(h)}(k)` in D24(b)'s norm.  No wave operator or completeness is presupposed.
