+# ML3 reconciliation against the S-IDX ladder
+
+**STATUS: NEGATIVE for Stage 2; positive route identified.**
+
+## ⟨1⟩1. Decision
+
+**ASSUME.**  “Load-bearing for the Letter” means necessary for a statement
+that the Letter presents as a theorem, rather than an explicitly open
+conjecture or a possible proof route.
+
+**PROVE.**  **ML3 is not load-bearing for the Letter's narrow proved
+protocol theorem.**  The exact theorem surface available without ML3 is:
+
+> For the fully polarised bilinear ferromagnet `H_S`, `2S∈ℕ`, on the
+> primitive regular two-magnon channel and the separated-preparation class
+> `(D29-HS-SEP)`, every actual row-measure limit subsequence obeys
+> `A_*(ε)=i sgn(v_h-v_s)\bar k_*(ε)/S+O(ε²)` and has phase slope
+> `sgn(v_h-v_s)/S`.
+
+The Letter may place this protocol theorem beside the finite Ward index, but
+must not say that the latter proves the former.  The Ward-to-running-protocol
+bridge `(PROTO-LSZ)` remains open.  ML3 remains load-bearing only for the
+stronger packet-smeared current route specified in ⟨1⟩3 below, not for the
+displayed narrow theorem.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-MATCH-HS-SEP`,
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`, `S2-2body-S`, and `S-IDX-fin-r2`.
+
+## ⟨1⟩2. Why the finite S-IDX theorem does not itself settle ML3
+
+**ASSUME.**  The full-sector and root-highest registers of the S-IDX ladder.
+
+**PROVE.**  The ladder separates a finite zero-mode identity from every
+running nonzero-soft-momentum statement.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  The finite theorem gives the descendant-range projection and
+normalized Ward index one; its pure zero-mode anchor explicitly makes no
+claim about the running protocol family.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-fin-r2` and `S-IDX-fin-G`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  General compact-group sector covariance gives a character-label
+difference, while the descendant projector is strictly finer than the
+target sector projector; labels therefore do not determine the projected
+current coefficient or a soft limit.
+
+*Justification.*  Claim `S-IDX-G-label`.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Consequently S-IDX-fin cannot be cited as a proof that a physical
+`1/k_s` current pole is absent.  It supplies the finite Ward numerator, not
+the uniform limiting estimate.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-fin-r2`, `S-IDX-fin-G`, and `ML3`.
+
+**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
+
+## ⟨1⟩3. Exact residual scope of ML3
+
+**ASSUME.**  Distinguish the whole-datum D29 matching route from the
+componentwise current/LSZ route.
+
+**PROVE.**  ML3 remains load-bearing for exactly the following stronger
+statement:
+
+> After packet smearing and the prescribed thermodynamic/soft limits, the
+> orthogonal-current component in a current spectral resolution is uniformly
+> regular at `k_s=0` (including `k_s=Θ(1/N)`), so it contributes no physical
+> `1/k_s` pole and is small enough for the descendant term alone to furnish
+> the leading Ward-derived soft law.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  This regularity is an explicit live premise of `S-general`, whose
+amplitudes and remainder use the D24(b) packet norm and D25 multiplier.
+
+*Justification.*  D24(b), D25, and claims `ML3` and `S-general`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  In the protocol ladder the analogous burden occurs inside
+`(PROTO-LSZ)`: the exhaustive component decomposition requires the
+orthogonal-current term to be `O(ε²)`.  Thus removing the name “ML3” from
+that ladder does not prove the estimate; a proof following the old spectral
+route would still have to discharge ML3's content.
+
+*Justification.*  D24(d)1--4 and claims `S-IDX-spec-struct-r2`, `ML3`, and
+`ML4-A`.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  The whole-datum separated-preparation route instead takes every
+soft scale fixed while constructing the two-body wave operators, sends the
+separation/settling indices out first, and takes `ε→0` last.  Its exact
+protocol/on-shell match therefore requires no bound uniform in `ε` and no
+componentwise current decomposition.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-MATCH-HS-SEP` and
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  Hence ML3 is not a dependency of the narrow protocol value, but
+it remains a dependency of `S-general` and a viable sufficient attack on the
+orthogonal-current clause needed to turn `S-IDX-spec-struct-r2` from a
+conditional statement into a microscopic Ward-derived protocol theorem.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-general`, `S-IDX-spec-struct-r2`,
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`, and `ML3`.
+
+**⟨2⟩5. QED.**
+
+## ⟨1⟩4. Premise-update audit
+
+**ASSUME.**  The brief's ML4-Ward erratum and the repaired D24(d)3 register.
+
+**PROVE.**  Neither update changes the decision.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  The refuted scalar display for `n≥2` cannot be used.  The finite
+root theorem keeps the full-sector Gram inverse, while the primitive
+one-hard consequence (R15) remains valid; the D29 whole-datum proof uses no
+`n≥2` scalar replacement.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `ML4-Ward`, `S-IDX-fin-G`, and
+`S-IDX-MATCH-HS-SEP`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  The repaired `𝒮_W(ρ)` class has no proved microscopic member and
+its amputation constant remains open.  This blocks the general
+Ward-derived factorisation, but not the narrow D29 value, which expressly
+makes no D24 membership or `𝔞_leg` claim.
+
+*Justification.*  D24(d) and claims `ML5-B`, `AMP`, and
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`.
+
+**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
+
+## ⟨1⟩5. Letter consequence and Stage 2 gate
+
+**ASSUME.**  The Letter keeps theorem labels no stronger than the claims DAG.
+
+**PROVE.**  The correct editorial split is:
+
+1. state the finite Ward index (`S-IDX-fin-r2`/`S-IDX-fin-G`) as proved;
+2. state the `(D29-HS-SEP)` protocol phase law as a separate proved,
+   model-specific theorem;
+3. label the Ward-to-running-protocol implication and `S-general` as open;
+4. do not list ML3 as a missing premise of item 2, but retain it under item 3.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-fin-r2`, `S-IDX-fin-G`,
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`, `S-IDX-spec-struct-r2`, and `S-general`.
+
+Because the Stage 1 answer is **not load-bearing for the Letter's narrow
+proved theorem**, the brief's Stage 2 condition is false.  No uniform-current
+proof is attempted in this lane.  The named forward attack is to use the
+whole-datum `(D29-HS-SEP)` bridge for the Letter and reserve ML3's Jacobi
+graph-norm/current-resolution program for a future promotion of the stronger
+Ward-derived or `n`-leg statement.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-MATCH-HS-SEP`,
+`S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`, `ML3`, and `S-general`.
+
+**⟨2⟩1. QED.**
+
+## ⟨1⟩6. QED
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  ML3 is removed only from the narrow Letter theorem's dependency
+surface; its stronger current-regularity claim is neither proved nor
+refuted.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `S-IDX-D29-value-HS-SEP`, `ML3`, and `S-general`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2. QED.**

